PART 3: THE NEW APPROACH - SINGLE PAGE APPLICATIONS (SPAs)

================================================================================

What is a Single Page Application?

A Single Page Application (SPA) is a web application where the application shell is loaded and JavaScript dynamically updates the UI rather than performing a full page navigation for every interaction.

SPA Characteristic         | Meaning
---------------------------|-------------------------------------------
Initial HTML/Application   | Loaded when application starts
Partial UI Updates         | Only required UI portions change
No Full Reload for Many UI | Interaction can happen client-side
Dynamic                    | JavaScript updates displayed content
Responsive                 | Can feel similar to desktop applications

Key Idea
ONE APPLICATION PAGE
        +
DYNAMIC JAVASCRIPT UPDATES
        =
SPA EXPERIENCE


================================================================================

HOW SPAs WORK

================================================================================

Initial Load
Step | Action
-----|----------------------------------------------
1    | User visits web application
2    | Browser requests application from server
3    | Server returns initial HTML/resources
4    | Browser loads the application
5    | JavaScript executes in browser


Flow:

USER
 ↓
BROWSER
 ↓
SERVER
 ↓
INITIAL APP
 ↓
JAVASCRIPT LOADS
 ↓
APPLICATION READY

After Initial Load - Local Interaction

For interactions that do not require server data:

Step | Action
-----|------------------------------------------------
1    | User clicks button
2    | JavaScript handles the event
3    | JavaScript updates required UI
4    | No full page reload is required
5    | User sees the change

When Server Data is Needed
Step | Action
-----|-------------------------------------------------
1    | User performs an action
2    | JavaScript sends request to server/API
3    | Server returns data, commonly JSON
4    | JavaScript processes the response
5    | Required UI is updated
6    | User sees updated information


Flow:

USER ACTION
     ↓
JAVASCRIPT
     ↓
FETCH / API REQUEST
     ↓
SERVER
     ↓
DATA / JSON
     ↓
JAVASCRIPT
     ↓
UPDATE REQUIRED UI


================================================================================

KEY DIFFERENCES: OLD VS NEW APPROACH

================================================================================

Feature          | Traditional Approach        | SPA Approach
-----------------|-----------------------------|------------------------------
Page Update      | Often full page navigation  | Specific UI can be updated
Rendering        | Often server-side           | Much UI handled client-side
Server Response  | Often HTML/page             | Often data such as JSON
Interaction      | More server round trips     | Many handled in browser
Visual Reload    | Can occur                   | Often avoided
User Experience  | Page-oriented               | More app-like


================================================================================

CODE EXAMPLE: NEW APPROACH - SPA STYLE

================================================================================

Initial HTML
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Counter App</title>
</head>
<body>

  <h1 id="counter">Counter: 5</h1>

  <button id="incrementBtn">
    Increment Counter
  </button>

  <script src="app.js"></script>

</body>
</html>

JavaScript
let count = 5;

const counterDisplay =
  document.getElementById('counter');

const incrementBtn =
  document.getElementById('incrementBtn');

incrementBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {

  count = count + 1;

  counterDisplay.textContent =
    `Counter: ${count}`;
});

What Happens When the User Clicks?
Step | Action
-----|-----------------------------------------------------
1    | JavaScript event listener detects click
2    | count increases from 5 to 6
3    | JavaScript updates only the counter element
4    | UI changes immediately
5    | No server request is needed for this local change
6    | No full page reload occurs
7    | User sees Counter: 6

Advantage
Counter: 5
    ↓
CLICK
    ↓
JavaScript
    ↓
Counter: 6

Only required UI changed.
No full page reload.


